				<title>SCP-5215</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5215</link>
				<description>

&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: right;&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Item #:&lt;/strong&gt; SCP-5215&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Object Class:&lt;/strong&gt; Keter&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Special Containment Procedures:&lt;/strong&gt; A perimeter has been established around SCP-5215 with an electric fence charged up to 300.000 volts, a metal gate at about 5 meters height using a magnetic seal lock, and sniper towers at every edge of the perimeter. Also at least 2 surveillance MQ-9 Reaper predator drones are to be present at the general air space of the containment site at all times. Should the site experience a power failure, on-site personnel are to utilize backup generators to reestablish communication with the active Security Chief as soon as possible. During an SCP-5215-2 instance, breach said instance is to be shot by one of the sniper towers which are equipped with anti-material rifles loaded with .308 Lapua rounds to terminate the subject. If the subject survives the shots, one of the on-site GCSs(Ground Control Stations) is to use predator drones to launch at least two AGM-114 Hellfire missiles. If more than 5 SCP-5215-2 instances reach the gate Mobile Task Force unit Nu-7 designated &amp;quot;Hammer Down&amp;quot; is to be dispatched with one goal which is to terminate the SCP-5215-2 instances as soon as possible because their extremely unpredictable behavior can cause damage to neighboring areas as well as a breach of secrecy to the foundation, with the one exception of SCP-5215-1(see addendum 5215-A for details).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Description:&lt;/strong&gt; SCP-5215 is a remote village named &amp;quot;Kaisariana&amp;quot; approximately ████ km south of the ████ border. At a first inspection, it looks like an ordinary village but when closer at about 100 meters from the entrance the subject enters a different dimension. In said dimension the subject(s) enter a comatose state for about 20-30 minutes, upon waking up observations show very light memory loss only including the last 12 hours of their life. Once awoken subjects are in a recovering state and can barely move. Once recovered their brain thinks that they were in this situation beforehand and were injured due to memory loss. Some of these &amp;quot;situations&amp;quot; are the following: World war 1 and 2, the Vietnam war, the cold war, the Afghanistan invasion, Iraq, etc. These anomalous events only occur under circumstances that are not yet known. The SCP-5215 population is around 70 people which are to be labeled SCP5215-2. Said subjects usually pass the age of 60 but all of them show advanced metabolism, motor skills, and huge life spans reaching up to 300000. Three of these inhabitants however retain abilities that can potentially cause a lot of damage should a total containment failure occur, therefore they are to be labeled SCP-5215-1 instances (check addendum 5215-A B and C). However, these SCP-5215-1 instances show to be more advanced at everything and potentially be immortal. Said instance is extremely hard to contain due to it being extremely resistant to most forms of physical damage, very intelligent, and immune to the effects of every other SCP.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Addendum:&lt;/strong&gt; Addendum: SCP-5215-A: SCP-5215-1-A is a humanoid male that goes by the name of &amp;quot;Κώστας Μαλουμίδης&amp;quot; and is approximately 457 years old, has immense knowledge of everything that has happened in the past 20 centuries. SCP-5215-1-A is extremely resistant to all kinds of damage with the exception of a substance called &amp;quot;Υγρόν πυρ&amp;quot; which slows him down and damages him enough forcing him to enter a dormant state for about 15 minutes. Because of the nature of SCP-5215-1-A containment breaches happen once or twice a month. Due to the immense amount of resources needed to re-contain SCP-5215-1-A, a termination request has been sent to the O5 council and is still awaiting confirmation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Addendum:&lt;/strong&gt; SCP-5215-1-B: SCP-5215-1-B is a humanoid male that goes by the name of &amp;quot;Τσάκος&amp;quot;.SCP-5215-1-A has control over every road in the SCP-5215. Other than this information not much is known about SCP-5215-1-B due to its anonymous nature.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Addendum:&lt;/strong&gt; SCP-5215-1-C: SCP-5215-1-C is a humanoid male that is named &amp;quot;Κιάρος&amp;quot; by the rest of the SCP-5215-1 and 2 instances. SCP-5215-1-C can control every type of vegetation, field, and garden in the village and is also the &amp;quot;supplier&amp;quot; according to the SCP-5215-2 instances that are not hostile.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Testing Logs:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
Test Log SCP-5215-Alpha: at ██/██/████, two D class personnel, D-2459, and D-3951, are given radios and navigators and are instructed to move closer to the village. At about 140 meters from the village, D-2459 reports a strange mist 40 meters from his position, though D-3951 reported nothing. D-2459 is ordered to proceed to the mist. When he reached the mist radio contact with D-2459 had been lost, therefore D-3951 was told to go search for D-2459. After 30 minutes D-3951 found D-2459 who had forgotten why he was there and was in a distressed state not being able to think straight. The test was called to a close and the class d personnel were called back due to lack of researchable material.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Results: New ability has been discovered.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Assessment: Further research is required.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Test Log SCP-5215-Beta:&lt;/strong&gt; D-8392 is sent 150 meters away from the entrance and is told to describe what he sees over the radio.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;quot;Looks like a village, I can see 4 people inside but it looks like a ghost town to me. Oh, I can see traffic now, for some reason the vehicles stop and start at random.&amp;quot;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;D-8392 is sent 100 meters away from the entrance and is told to keep walking no matter what. He is given a note that says &amp;quot;You are in a test, please write down everything that you see on this paper, after that take a walk around, describe what you see and come back from the main road&amp;quot;. D-6721 is sent 150 meters away from the entrance and is told to observe D-8392.&lt;br /&gt;
D-6721 reports seeing D-8392 collapse and stay like that for 25 minutes. After said time subject is reported to wake up, extremely distressed. Radio communication with D-8392 is lost. The subject takes a note out of his pocket, reads it, and proceeds to use a pen that was put in his pocket to take notes after 3 minutes subject starts walking around and is no longer able to be seen by D-6721, who reports she only sees fog after a certain distance. Subject D-8392 after 20 minutes returns to D-6721. Both subjects return to the researcher team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;D-8392&#039;s note:&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;quot;I can see some dirt roads and a few houses, dogs are also running around here. I saw an old man walking around, kinda creepy considering he was alone in the streets. I asked him what this place is and if anyone else lives here, he said the village is a small one but people do live here, although he looked uncomfortable when I questioned him about the nature of this place in particular. He said trucks come here every few days to bring supplies, owned by a guy familiar around here named &amp;quot;████&amp;quot;. Apparently, he&#039;s some kind of farmer who owns a company or something I don&#039;t know. I can see someone in the distance, I will update you. I&#039;m safe now, I can see Helen in the distance, I don&#039;t remember these numbers you guys are giving us. Anyways, this old man, I can only describe him as bald, with a unibrow and, heck I don&#039;t know if he&#039;s crazy or not. He started chasing me with a tree log. The other citizen didn&#039;t even seem to care. What the fuck.&amp;quot;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Test Log SCP-5215-Charlie: Two Class-D personnel, D-7193, and D-9185 are instructed to enter SCP-5215 and attempt to make contact with SCP-5215-1-A to learn something new about it. One hour in both D-7193 and D-9185 report that they saw a strange humanoid entity roaming the streets of SCP-5215 so they are instructed by the researcher team to approach it. Upon closer inspection, the entity was SCP-5215-1-A, and immediately after reaching it, the entity released a liquid acid-like substance on both D class personnel. Shortly after both of them were dead. Thirty seconds later SCP-5215-1-B appeared out of an abandoned house and started shaping roads for the substance to flow downhill towards the researchers. Minutes later SCP-5215-1-A and B alongside 50 SCP-5215-2 instances attempted to breach containment using the acid as cover for their advance. Mobile Task Force unit Nu-7 designated &amp;quot;Hammer Down&amp;quot; entered the containment site and were outnumbered and couldn&#039;t proceed due to the large amounts of acid. The active Security Chief requested the deployment of Mobile Task Force unit Beta-7 designated &amp;quot;Maz Hatters to clear the acid so MTF could proceed with the elimination of all SCP-5215-2 instances and attempt to re contain SCP-5215-1-A and B. One hour later all SCP-5215-2 instances were eliminated and SCP-5215-1-A and B retreated to SCP-5215.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Results: More than 10 MTF soldiers were eliminated 34 were injured and two helicopters were bought down by SCP-5215-A. Though samples of the acid were collected by Mobile Task Force unit Beta-7 and research is undergoing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;#171; &lt;a href=&quot;http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5214&quot;&gt;SCP-5214&lt;/a&gt; | SCP-5215 | &lt;a href=&quot;http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5216&quot;&gt;SCP-5216&lt;/a&gt; &amp;#187;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;by &lt;span class=&quot;printuser avatarhover&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/splatink&quot;  &gt;&lt;img class=&quot;small&quot; src=&quot;http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=6345322&amp;amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;amp;timestamp=1606489128&quot; alt=&quot;Splatink&quot; style=&quot;background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=6345322)&quot; /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/splatink&quot;  &gt;Splatink&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
</description>
